The Macroassembler AS is a portable macro cross assembler for a
variety of microprocessors and -controllers.  Though it is mainly
targeted at embedded processors and single-board computers,
you also find CPU families in the target list that are used in
workstations and PCs.

Most UNIX systems name their own assembler already 'as', so the name
of the AS was modified to 'asl'.  The additional letter is to the
honor of a person that did quite a lot to spread the UNIX philosophy.
